MIKA
Mikey is not able to sell the house, he listens to you and prices it way to high, and he get exactly no one interested in looking at the house.  I know this kid, we know this kid, we know exactly what he is capable of.

NONA
He sold Mideas house.  Two weeks.  Two weeks and the house was sold.  We will have no problems.  None.

MIKA
Oh come on.  Midea's house was perfect.  Perfect.  Updated kitchen, huge yard, you could fit three cars in that garage.  I could have sold that house.  Easy to do.  Your parent's house, this house, not easy.

Nona smiles confidently again after a sip of coffee.

NONA
No.  No. This house is perfect.  It is great. There will be no problems. 

MIKA
It is not great.  Not great.  Not not great.  It's good, it's a good house, yes.  But it has problems.

NONA
Like what?

MIKA
Like the fact the kitchen is out of a 1970s Reader's Digest advertisement.  Like the fact there are three bathrooms with pink tiles.  Pink tiles.  Three. Like the fact every square inch of flooring that is not bathroom is carpeting from the 1980s.

NONA
You can stop now.  I do not need to listen to this.  This house - 

She pauses to sip coffee

NONA
This house, is perfect.  It will sell.  Besides, I have already called Mikey.

MIKA
How? When? Why did you do this and not ask me?

Nona speaks perfect English with no accent.

NONA
Um, because, I do not need your permission.  It is my house. I make the deicisions.

MIKA
You do not need my permission that is not what I said. 

NONA
Sure sounded like it.

MIKA
Not my permission, just my advice.

NONA
